\tag{fdip}
\title{Calculus on a finite set}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{How can the functions on a finite set carry a differential, a product
rule, and an integral, when the ground ring is only assumed commutative?}

\p{The classification of first-order calculi and the product rule come
first. Higher-degree forms are compared with the cochains of a torus,
and the weighted integral is compared with Stokes' theorem.}

